  },
  "kokoro": "The 'kokoro' field is misaki notation, NOT standard IPA -- misaki writes /ai/ as 'I', /au/ as 'W', /ou/ as 'O', /ei/ as 'A'. Every value here was produced by misaki itself, so it is guaranteed in-vocabulary; hand-written IPA passes through the G2P without an error and then lands out-of-distribution at the model, which is silent corruption. 'kokoro_never_disambiguates' marks words where the G2P returned the SAME phonemes for both senses -- measured 2026-09-01, so those always need the model."
 },
